' 06 Commit of a space transaction: SpaceTxn::commit as an activity.
'
' Source of Figure S5.2 in ../design.md (section S5.2). The figure restates
' HostTxn::commit, commit_staged and commit_operation in
' rspace++/src/rspace/space_store_handle.rs, and the apply_op of
' PlayBackend (rspace/space_play.rs) and of ReplayBackend
' (replay_rspace/space_replay.rs). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The commit refuses a closed transaction, takes what begin holds, and
'      clears the staged pairings and the counter delta.
'   2. Two checks run before any operation: the hot store must be the one of
'      begin, and the parent order must be fresh in the evaluation scope.
'   3. Each staged operation i runs under sub_order(parent, i): read-only
'      checks, the host call sequence of its mode, and the event correlation.
'      In replay, an unpaired fire makes the observer calls of play and then
'      fails with ReplayDivergence, before any event (decision 36).
'   4. Every error after the take step releases the locks and then the
'      registration. An error of operation i leaves operations 0 to i - 1
'      applied (prefix atomicity).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 06-space-txn-commit.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 06-space-txn-commit
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Commit of a space transaction: SpaceTxn::commit

start
:commit() on an open HostTxn; <<$rrs_substrate>>
if (the transaction is open?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :fail with **Finished**
  no effect; <<$rrs_reject>>
  stop
endif
:take the locks and the registration
mark the transaction finished
clear the paired COMM events and <latex>\delta</latex>; <<$rrs_substrate>>
if (the captured hot store is the current one?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :fail with **StoreSwapped**
  no effect; <<$rrs_reject>>
  :release the locks, then the registration; <<$rrs_substrate>>
  stop
endif
if (an operation order is current?) then (yes: parent)
  if (parent path already committed in this evaluation scope?) then (no)
    :record the parent path (FR-5'); <<$rrs_substrate>>
  else (yes)
    :fail with **ParentOrderReused**
    no effect; <<$rrs_reject>>
    :release the locks, then the registration; <<$rrs_substrate>>
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  :commit untracked, with no sub-orders; <<$rrs_substrate>>
endif
while (next staged operation i, in staging order?) is (yes)
  partition "Operation i under <latex>\mathit{parent} \mathbin{+\!\!+} [(i, 2)]</latex>" {
    :read-only checks of the changed entries (FR-7'):
    joins of the produce channel unchanged,
    room in the host counter of a non-persistent produce,
    <latex>\mathrm{live\_comm} = \mathrm{staged\ COMM}</latex>,
    removed entries at their staged positions; <<$rrs_substrate>>
    if (a check fails?) then (yes)
      :fail with **Inconsistent** or **CounterOverflow**
      operations 0 to i - 1 stay applied; <<$rrs_reject>>
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
    :before_observe(source): the authority registration of the reducer; <<$rrs_agent>>
    :start_accounting_operation(source, channels, joins); <<$rrs_host>>
    if (replay or reporting, and the observer returns a directive?) then (yes)
      :fail with **NativeReplayDirectiveUnsupported**
      observer finish: Rejected, operations 0 to i - 1 stay applied; <<$rrs_reject>>
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
    :observe_produce or observe_consume; <<$rrs_host>>
    if (replay produce?) then (yes)
      :increment_produce_counter; <<$rrs_host>>
    else (no)
    endif
    switch (outcome of operation i)
    case (Store)
      :log_produce, then store_data:
      put_datum at the head of the list; <<$rrs_storage>>
    case (Park)
      :log_consume, then store_waiting_continuation:
      put_continuation, then put_join for each channel; <<$rrs_storage>>
    case (Fire)
      :observe_comm with the staged COMM; <<$rrs_host>>
      if (replay or reporting, and the fire is unpaired (recorded = none)?) then (yes)
        :fail with **ReplayDivergence** (decision 36)
        after the observer calls of play: no event,
        no store change, no binding change,
        and a produce rolls its counter step back
        observer finish: Rejected, operations 0 to i - 1 stay applied; <<$rrs_reject>>
        stop
      else (no: paired, or play)
      endif
      :log the produce or consume event, then the COMM event
      (play: the event log, replay: the logger); <<$rrs_host>>
      :remove a non-persistent continuation (produce side)
      remove the stored non-persistent records,
      also for a peek fire (decision 45)
      remove the fired joins
      the incoming datum is never stored (FR-10); <<$rrs_storage>>
      :replay and reporting: remove_bindings_for(COMM); <<$rrs_host>>
    endswitch
    :observe_operation_finish: Stored or Matched; <<$rrs_host>>
    :correlate the staged effects with the events of operation i; <<$rrs_substrate>>
    if (an effect lacks its event?) then (yes)
      :fail with **EventCoverage**, a defect
      operations 0 to i stay applied; <<$rrs_reject>>
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
    :receipt i: Stored, Parked, or Fired; <<$rrs_substrate>>
  }
endwhile (no more)
:release the locks, then the registration; <<$rrs_substrate>>
:return the receipts in staging order; <<$rrs_substrate>>
stop

note right
**Host errors** (OutOfPhlogistons, HostWorkRejected,
an authority conflict) can reject operation i at
before_observe, at the observer start, or at an observe
call. Operation i then logs no event and changes no
store entry, and operations 0 to i - 1 stay applied.
A failed replay fire rolls its counter back.
An unpaired replay fire makes the calls of play, so
a rejected call gives the error and the cost of play.
After every error, the commit releases the locks
and then the registration.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_substrate>  | substrate of P1: checks and bookkeeping |
|<$rrs_host>       | host call at the baseline: observer, events, bindings |
|<$rrs_storage>    | effect on the hot store |
|<$rrs_agent>      | callback of the space agent |
|<$rrs_reject>     | failure: the commit stops |
endlegend
@enduml
